---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {datasetEntries,datasetSchema,snapshotDate,scopeNote,snapshot,snapshotVersion,snapshotAmount,siteUrl} from '../../lib/discovery';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'DataCatalog',name:'Chicago Budget 2026 public-data catalog',description:scopeNote,url:`${siteUrl}/datasets/`,publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Chicago Budget',url:siteUrl},dataset:datasetEntries.map(datasetSchema)};
---
<Base title="2026 public budget datasets" description="Download the versioned Chicago City, CPS and Park District 2026 budget tree and inspect source citations, checksums and terms.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Datasets</nav>
  <section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Public data</p><h1>2026 budget datasets</h1><p class="lede">Explore three separately published budget trees, their original sources and the reproducible download snapshot. This independent project is not a government publisher.</p></section>
  <p>{scopeNote}</p><p>Published download snapshot generated <time datetime={snapshotDate}>{snapshotDate}</time>. Snapshot export version <code>{snapshotVersion}</code> from its own <a href={`${snapshot}/site/manifest.json`}>site manifest</a>; the current interactive site's export may be newer. Amounts in source JSON are integer cents, not dollars. The <a href={`${snapshot}/catalog.json`}>publication catalog</a> lists SHA-256 checksums, original paths and byte counts per file. Download in GitHub rather than duplicating hundreds of megabytes on this site.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><caption>Separate 2026 government budgets in the published snapshot</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Dataset</th><th scope="col">Period</th><th scope="col">Root amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>{datasetEntries.map(entry=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={`/datasets/2026/${entry.slug}/`}>{entry.name}</a></th><td>{entry.period}</td><td>{snapshotAmount(entry.root)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <h2>How to use the release</h2><ol><li>Read the <a href={`${snapshot}/tree/manifest.json`}>tree manifest</a> for category paths and the <a href={`${snapshot}/tree/lookup.json`}>box lookup</a> for each box ID and its citation.</li><li>Read <a href={`${snapshot}/site/manifest.json`}>site manifest</a> and chunks for the exact website data representation.</li><li>Check <a href={`${snapshot}/catalog.json`}>catalog checksums</a> before processing downloaded files, then consult the <a href="https://github.com/gettty/chicagobudget/blob/main/data/README.md">download guide</a>.</li></ol>
  <p>The <a href={`${snapshot}/sources/`}>original-input layer</a> preserves public-source names that are intentionally omitted from website pages. Its publisher terms remain distinct; this site does not grant a blanket license over government records. See <a href="https://github.com/gettty/chicagobudget/blob/main/LICENSES.md">license and source terms</a>. <a href="/guides/">Read the budget explainers</a>.</p>
</Base>
